From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: soc: sunxi: cpu_comm: the thread word of a held lock must not read as "free"

The software spinlocks shared with the display MIPS (0259) write the holding
thread into the entry's thread word, and both sides test that word to tell a
free lock: the firmware looks at its low byte being 0xff (tridspinlock.c:326),
this side at the whole word being 255. The word written was the bare tgid.

So a process with pid 255 held routine lock 2 with a thread word that read
"free" to both sides. Its own unlock skipped ("SpinUnLock(2): no thread_id"),
the lock stayed ARM-owned with ref 1 for ever, the MIPS waited on it without
a timeout, every open of the HDMI receiver was refused ("the callbacks cannot
be registered (-16)") and the wall stayed dark until h713-tv-rescue reloaded
the MIPS (TODO 2.67; 2.63 before 0259 had the same seed: the MIPS taking a
lock this side held). h713-tv is the process that registers first after a
warm start, and it gets pid 255 in about one boot of twenty -- 1 of 20 on
11.10., 2 of 21 on 12.10., both traced step by step (arbeit/wurzeln-20261012,
L2T trace: "lock: taken ... own=0 ref=1 tid=000000ff", pid 255). Pids 511,
767, ... would have let the MIPS take a lock this side held.

The tgid moves up one byte and the low byte is a constant that is not 0xff.
pid_max is far below 2^24. Nothing else reads the word as a pid: the RPC
channel id has its own thread field.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_hw.c
@@ -1054,11 +1054,30 @@
  * Returns 2 = taken, 1 = taken again by the holding thread, 0 = held
  * elsewhere (mode 0 only), negative errno = not taken.
  */
+/*
+ * The thread word this side writes into an entry it holds. Not the bare
+ * tgid: the firmware's test for "free" is the LOW BYTE of the thread word
+ * being 0xff (tridspinlock.c:326, re-auftrag/BERICHT.md 1.4), and this
+ * side's own test in comm_SpinUnLock() is the whole word being 255. A
+ * process with pid 255 -- h713-tv gets it in about one warm start of twenty
+ * -- therefore held routine lock 2 with a thread word that read "free" to
+ * both sides: its own unlock skipped ("no thread_id"), the lock stayed
+ * ARM-owned for ever, every open of the HDMI receiver was refused and the
+ * wall stayed dark until h713-tv-rescue (TODO 2.67, L2T trace of
+ * 12.10.2026, arbeit/wurzeln-20261012). Pids 511, 767, ... would have let
+ * the MIPS take a lock this side held. So the tgid moves up a byte and the
+ * low byte is a constant that is not 0xff; pid_max is far below 2^24.
+ */
+static u32 spinlock_thread_id(void)
+{
+	return ((u32)current->tgid << 8) | 0x01;
+}
+
 static int spinLock(int lock_id, int mode)
 {
 	void __iomem *e;
 	unsigned long deadline = jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(SPINLOCK_HOLD_TIMEOUT_MS);
-	u32 tid = (u32)current->tgid;
+	u32 tid = spinlock_thread_id();
 	u32 old_tid;
 	int ref, ret;
 	u8 cpu;
